WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.015
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:13.285 --> 00:15.175
Hello, Miwa?

3
00:16.645 --> 00:18.915
Yeah, I just got off work.

4
00:21.085 --> 00:22.315
How was the reunion?

5
00:25.185 --> 00:26.555
I snuck out early.

6
00:28.995 --> 00:30.295
Did something happen?

7
00:32.695 --> 00:33.725
Nothing.

8
00:34.325 --> 00:35.435
Nothing at all.

9
00:37.335 --> 00:39.655
Didn't you run into that girl you used to have a crush on?

10
00:42.575 --> 00:43.875
I did.

11
00:45.445 --> 00:46.875
It was pretty ordinary, though.

12
00:48.375 --> 00:49.375
By the way,

13
00:49.415 --> 00:50.715
is it really loud over there?

14
00:50.725 --> 00:52.045
Where are you right now?

15
00:55.185 --> 00:56.185
Listen,

16
00:58.085 --> 01:00.025
can I come see you right now?

17
01:00.825 --> 01:02.065
Huh? Why?

18
01:04.125 --> 01:05.395
No reason.

19
01:06.865 --> 01:08.235
I just really want to see you.

20
01:09.465 --> 01:10.465
Or rather,

21
01:11.765 --> 01:13.505
I felt like I couldn't not see you.

22
01:16.005 --> 01:17.535
So can we meet up now?

23
01:55.505 --> 02:03.005
"How Do We Relationship?"

24
02:08.005 --> 02:13.805
(Episode 5: No Matter Where You Run, No Matter Where You Hide)

25
02:16.435 --> 02:17.235
Sorry to keep you waiting.

26
02:17.236 --> 02:18.505
Good work today.

27
02:18.565 --> 02:19.804
Did you order anything yet?

28
02:19.805 --> 02:21.704
Not yet, just drinks for now.

29
02:21.705 --> 02:22.705
Thanks.

30
02:27.745 --> 02:28.845
What's up?

31
02:29.245 --> 02:30.545
Nothing. It's nothing.

32
02:30.675 --> 02:33.515
Come on, now I'm curious. Spit it out.

33
02:36.615 --> 02:38.985
Just wondering why you suddenly came to see me today.

34
02:39.005 --> 02:40.855
You never used to do that before.

35
02:41.395 --> 02:42.395
Well...

36
02:42.825 --> 02:45.995
Maybe... I thought seeing you would put my mind at ease.

37
02:46.525 --> 02:48.725
I don't know why, but I'm just kind of exhausted today.

38
02:48.795 --> 02:49.864
Really?

39
02:49.865 --> 02:50.865
Yeah.

40
02:51.335 --> 02:56.535
You know how you're always saying silly things to make me laugh?

41
02:56.735 --> 03:00.145
Can I take that as a compliment?

42
03:00.275 --> 03:02.775
I wish I were more like you.

43
03:02.785 --> 03:06.045
Good at lying and knowing how to handle people.

44
03:06.515 --> 03:08.755
Ouch, you make me sound awful.

45
03:09.085 --> 03:10.985
I-I'm sorry, Saeko.

46
03:11.285 --> 03:13.585
I just meant you're tactful and good with people.

47
03:14.055 --> 03:16.525
I'll never forgive you for that.

48
03:16.955 --> 03:18.725
I'll pay for tonight, okay?

49
03:21.965 --> 03:22.965
Deal.

50
03:23.035 --> 03:24.035
You're forgiven.

51
03:24.495 --> 03:25.905
I'll go get us drinks.

52
03:38.715 --> 03:43.555
I want us to go back to how we were before.

53
03:45.085 --> 03:46.625
I'm sorry for being so selfish.

54
03:47.425 --> 03:48.425
But...

55
03:48.695 --> 03:50.555
that's the whole reason I came today.

56
03:52.965 --> 03:55.365
How we were before...?

57
03:57.185 --> 03:59.165
Well, let's see.

58
03:59.705 --> 04:01.935
We could talk about anything,

59
04:02.505 --> 04:04.335
feel totally comfortable around each other...

60
04:04.475 --> 04:06.305
Like a really close junior?

61
04:07.705 --> 04:10.274
Wait, wouldn't that just make me a normal underclassman?

62
04:10.275 --> 04:11.914
Not at all.

63
04:11.915 --> 04:15.185
You've always been someone special to me.

64
04:18.155 --> 04:20.585
Meeting you back then, Inuzuka,

65
04:21.455 --> 04:23.195
made me who I am today.

66
04:24.295 --> 04:26.365
It's all thanks to you.

67
04:28.735 --> 04:31.465
Thanks to me?

68
04:33.635 --> 04:38.775
You really still don't realize how much what you did meant to me, do you?

69
04:41.715 --> 04:43.745
Inuzuka, you're the one who made my life

70
04:43.945 --> 04:45.785
feel completely invincible.

71
04:46.145 --> 04:47.665
Will you take responsibility for that?

72
05:00.925 --> 05:03.435
Oh, you're back.

73
05:04.935 --> 05:06.105
By the way,

74
05:06.265 --> 05:08.475
we never did make it to the beach.

75
05:08.875 --> 05:10.305
Yeah, that's true.

76
05:11.205 --> 05:13.004
Want to go on our next date?

77
05:13.005 --> 05:15.275
Isn't it a bit late in the season for swimming, though?

78
05:15.315 --> 05:17.844
It's still fun just looking at the ocean.

79
05:17.845 --> 05:20.785
Really? You think it'll be fun?

80
05:21.385 --> 05:23.085
It'll be great!

81
05:23.385 --> 05:25.655
Oh, right! Miwa.

82
05:26.055 --> 05:27.055
Yeah?

83
05:27.225 --> 05:28.595
Help me write some lyrics!

84
05:28.625 --> 05:31.994
I tried writing some, but they're not working at all!

85
05:31.995 --> 05:34.764
What? No way, I've never written lyrics before!

86
05:34.765 --> 05:37.595
Don't worry, just write from the heart!

87
05:39.535 --> 05:40.205
Wait...

88
05:40.206 --> 05:43.475
Isn't this a love song?

89
05:43.775 --> 05:44.775
Yep!

90
05:45.445 --> 05:49.975
If the two of us team up, we'll write the ultimate love song!

91
05:52.415 --> 05:54.285
You won't laugh at me for being cheesy, right?

92
05:54.305 --> 05:56.785
I won't laugh, promise.

93
05:57.815 --> 05:58.825
Come on, please?

94
06:01.425 --> 06:02.695
All right, but...

95
06:02.895 --> 06:04.865
what should I write?

96
06:15.775 --> 06:18.074
"A warmth in my chest..."

97
06:18.075 --> 06:19.604
"So warm."

98
06:19.605 --> 06:21.314
- That's so cute. - Okay, that's enough!

99
06:21.315 --> 06:22.334
- But it's great! - Stop looking at it!

100
06:22.335 --> 06:23.534
Don't read it out loud!

101
06:23.535 --> 06:25.391
- Now let me see what you wrote! - Wait, hold on!

102
06:25.415 --> 06:26.785
No, no, no!

103
06:51.405 --> 06:53.975
We ended up staying up all night until morning.

104
06:54.205 --> 06:56.775
And we didn't get any lyrics written at all.

105
06:57.775 --> 06:59.585
Let's write together again sometime.

106
06:59.785 --> 07:00.785
Sounds good.

107
07:02.555 --> 07:03.955
Hey,

108
07:05.085 --> 07:07.285
there's something I need to apologize to you for, Miwa.

109
07:07.655 --> 07:08.655
Huh?

110
07:09.155 --> 07:10.155
For what?

111
07:11.095 --> 07:12.095
To be honest,

112
07:12.865 --> 07:15.235
I kind of doubted you earlier.

113
07:16.995 --> 07:17.995
What?

114
07:18.765 --> 07:23.305
I mean, anyone would be suspicious after that phone call.

115
07:23.535 --> 07:25.695
I thought you were cheating on me with your old crush.

116
07:25.735 --> 07:26.695
I'd never cheat on you!

117
07:26.696 --> 07:27.776
That's why I'm telling you,

118
07:28.245 --> 07:30.475
it was all just in my head.

119
07:32.615 --> 07:34.245
It was wrong of me to doubt you.

120
07:36.415 --> 07:37.415
So...

121
07:38.285 --> 07:39.285
Mm...

122
07:40.325 --> 07:41.325
Hm?

123
07:42.595 --> 07:43.595
What is it?

124
07:43.825 --> 07:45.065
What do you mean, 'what is it'?

125
07:45.665 --> 07:47.725
I'm waiting for a kiss, obviously.

126
07:48.565 --> 07:49.565
Huh?

127
07:50.165 --> 07:50.935
Right here?

128
07:50.936 --> 07:52.635
Nobody else is around!

129
07:54.905 --> 07:55.905
Yeah, but...

130
07:56.135 --> 07:57.575
Miwa,

131
07:58.005 --> 08:00.845
didn't you come all the way out here to see me because you like me?

132
08:02.815 --> 08:04.345
If you like me, then kiss me.

133
08:09.385 --> 08:10.885
Shoot, someone's coming.

134
08:31.055 --> 08:32.174
Good work.

135
08:32.175 --> 08:33.175
Good work.

136
08:33.645 --> 08:36.015
Huh? What's up, Sae-chan?

137
08:36.575 --> 08:37.475
Why the face?

138
08:37.545 --> 08:42.784
Like, "Something happened between my partner and her ex-crush, and things are a total mess"?

139
08:42.785 --> 08:43.675
Huh?

140
08:43.676 --> 08:45.425
I don't look like that at all!

141
08:45.655 --> 08:49.075
Oh, right, I hear a new part-timer is starting today.

142
08:49.355 --> 08:50.625
Oh, really?

143
08:50.635 --> 08:51.635
Yeah.

144
09:14.915 --> 09:15.915
Hello, everyone!

145
09:17.855 --> 09:20.925
I'm Washio. I'm starting work here today.

146
09:23.055 --> 09:24.055
Yasa...?

147
09:24.295 --> 09:25.495
Yasa-chan?

148
09:26.365 --> 09:27.725
Nope!

149
09:27.765 --> 09:29.535
It's the 'Yu' in Yuria!

150
09:31.735 --> 09:32.735
Anyway,

151
09:33.265 --> 09:35.335
what's the deal with this mannequin head?

152
09:36.105 --> 09:37.105
Oh, this?

153
09:38.005 --> 09:40.475
This is Ashida-san.

154
09:41.745 --> 09:44.715
I'm attending beauty school right now,

155
09:44.845 --> 09:48.215
and Ashida-san and I practice all sorts of techniques together.

156
09:48.585 --> 09:50.985
She's kind of like my partner in crime.

157
09:54.155 --> 09:55.325
Nice to meet you...

158
09:58.015 --> 10:01.735
Ashida-san...

159
10:07.135 --> 10:08.605
Ashida-san!

160
10:10.275 --> 10:11.275
For some reason,

161
10:11.276 --> 10:13.505
Yuria just completely cracks me up.

162
10:13.605 --> 10:17.045
Hey, don't laugh at me!

163
10:17.645 --> 10:20.185
I feel like I haven't laughed this hard in ages.

164
10:25.055 --> 10:26.055
Sorry.

165
10:26.925 --> 10:28.125
Listen,

166
10:28.725 --> 10:29.725
I think...

167
10:30.395 --> 10:32.425
I might be coming down with a cold today.

168
10:33.565 --> 10:34.935
Oh, really?

169
10:35.765 --> 10:37.835
You should get to bed early tonight, then.

170
10:37.935 --> 10:38.935
Good night.

171
10:47.305 --> 10:48.815
Saeko.

172
10:49.875 --> 10:50.975
I'm sorry.

173
10:51.885 --> 10:53.745
I'm not mad at you.

174
10:54.085 --> 10:57.355
Just get to sleep early and rest up.

175
10:58.555 --> 10:59.555
Okay.

176
11:07.935 --> 11:09.035
I'm really sorry.

177
11:18.945 --> 11:21.075
This place is completely deserted!

178
11:22.275 --> 11:24.245
That's your takeaway from coming to the beach?

179
11:24.415 --> 11:26.585
There really is nothing out here!

180
11:28.055 --> 11:30.115
Isn't it nice that there's nothing here?

181
11:30.215 --> 11:32.285
Not at all!

182
11:32.785 --> 11:36.125
Want to go somewhere else?

183
11:40.495 --> 11:43.895
No way. Miwa went through the trouble of bringing me here.

184
12:11.175 --> 12:12.175
Miwa.

185
12:12.235 --> 12:13.235
Look over here.

186
12:17.335 --> 12:21.305
I'm a crab!

187
12:26.075 --> 12:27.875
What are you doing all of a sudden?

188
12:28.115 --> 12:30.245
There's that smile!

189
12:31.615 --> 12:32.615
Huh?

190
12:33.145 --> 12:36.385
You've had a gloomy look on your face lately, Miwa.

191
12:39.285 --> 12:40.925
I have not.

192
12:41.495 --> 12:42.725
Really?

193
12:43.255 --> 12:47.395
Well, it feels like forever since I saw you smile. I'm glad I did.

194
12:52.165 --> 12:53.465
What are you talking about?

195
12:55.535 --> 12:58.205
I smile all the time.

196
13:14.225 --> 13:15.255
Why...

197
13:18.195 --> 13:20.495
Why are you so sweet to me?

198
13:31.105 --> 13:32.974
Whoa! That's freezing!

199
13:32.975 --> 13:34.305
It's so cold!

200
13:36.645 --> 13:38.544
Wait, don't splash me!

201
13:38.545 --> 13:40.864
That's what you get for crying out of nowhere!

202
13:40.865 --> 13:42.855
That's your punishment for startling me!

203
13:45.185 --> 13:46.185
I know, but...

204
13:46.725 --> 13:48.424
I don't know why.

205
13:48.425 --> 13:50.294
Maybe it's being at the ocean?

206
13:50.295 --> 13:51.764
Come on.

207
13:51.765 --> 13:55.665
If you're gonna cry every time we come to the beach, that's going to be a problem.

208
14:01.475 --> 14:03.035
Hey, Saeko.

209
14:03.975 --> 14:06.505
Let's come to the beach together next year, too.

210
14:07.845 --> 14:09.645
Next year, huh?

211
14:10.615 --> 14:13.515
Will we still be dating by then?

212
14:17.215 --> 14:18.215
What?

213
14:19.825 --> 14:21.925
Man, my feet are totally numb.

214
14:22.255 --> 14:23.725
Let's get out of the water.

215
14:28.935 --> 14:30.235
We will be.

216
14:30.435 --> 14:31.605
The two of us.

217
14:32.705 --> 14:34.065
Next year, too.

218
14:37.475 --> 14:40.005
We're never breaking up.

219
14:41.645 --> 14:42.945
Never?

220
14:43.345 --> 14:44.645
Why are you so sure?

221
14:46.615 --> 14:47.915
Because...

222
14:50.585 --> 14:53.085
I don't want to let you go.

223
14:55.995 --> 14:59.065
Who else would ever want to date someone like me

224
14:59.725 --> 15:01.595
except for you, Saeko?

225
15:06.105 --> 15:07.635
That's just...

226
15:09.105 --> 15:10.305
Besides...

227
15:11.475 --> 15:15.645
I'm always taking from you,

228
15:15.715 --> 15:17.575
and I haven't given you anything in return.

229
15:19.885 --> 15:21.415
Your kindness,

230
15:22.555 --> 15:23.815
your trust,

231
15:24.745 --> 15:26.255
your affection...

232
15:26.845 --> 15:28.295
All of it.

233
15:33.595 --> 15:37.035
Next year and the year after that won't even be enough to make it up to you.

234
15:37.085 --> 15:38.085
So...

235
15:46.305 --> 15:48.975
You're way too serious, Miwa.

236
15:55.015 --> 15:56.931
You haven't been coming to band practice lately.

237
15:56.955 --> 15:57.855
Huh?

238
15:57.925 --> 15:58.925
What about it?

239
15:59.085 --> 16:00.765
Did something happen between you and Miwa?

240
16:01.025 --> 16:02.025
What?

241
16:02.525 --> 16:03.755
Nothing happened.

242
16:05.695 --> 16:06.925
Yeah, right.

243
16:08.735 --> 16:10.635
Did Miwa say something?

244
16:12.305 --> 16:14.005
No, she didn't say anything.

245
16:14.875 --> 16:16.505
Not that she'd confide in me anyway.

246
16:16.935 --> 16:18.605
But something's definitely up, right?

247
16:18.875 --> 16:20.275
Just like back at training camp.

248
16:21.375 --> 16:22.375
No,

249
16:22.875 --> 16:25.945
really, nothing happened.

250
16:26.245 --> 16:28.815
Besides, isn't that just how couples are?

251
16:29.455 --> 16:31.685
Things get awkward out of nowhere,

252
16:31.725 --> 16:33.885
and then work themselves out eventually.

253
16:34.125 --> 16:36.595
Isn't it exhausting getting hung up on every little thing?

254
16:38.765 --> 16:41.695
It's easier to just let things slide.

255
16:43.935 --> 16:45.765
Isn't that what dating is?

256
16:48.505 --> 16:49.505
Whatever.

257
16:50.575 --> 16:52.545
I don't know what's going on,

258
16:53.175 --> 16:55.915
but just apologize to Miwa and get back to practice already.

259
16:56.145 --> 16:57.745
Everyone's worried about you.

260
16:59.085 --> 17:03.055
I told you, we didn't fight.

261
17:03.115 --> 17:04.855
Yeah, yeah, fine.

262
17:05.385 --> 17:07.385
Just come back once you've sorted yourself out.

263
17:08.725 --> 17:10.155
I'm heading out.

264
17:35.105 --> 17:38.305
(Sawatari Saeko: Sorry, can't make it today!)

265
17:51.505 --> 17:55.305
(Kumagai Shiho: It was so wonderful seeing you after so long! I'm really glad we got to talk.)

266
18:07.585 --> 18:09.185
Ugh, I hate that noise.

267
18:09.315 --> 18:11.154
That thud is annoying too.

268
18:11.155 --> 18:12.685
Could you stop making so much noise?

269
18:13.355 --> 18:15.315
How many days in a row have you worked, Sae-chan?

270
18:16.525 --> 18:18.525
Six days straight, isn't it?

271
18:18.665 --> 18:20.724
Haven't you been pushing yourself a little too hard lately?

272
18:20.725 --> 18:22.265
You look completely drained, too.

273
18:22.465 --> 18:25.205
Wait, are things on the rocks with your partner?

274
18:30.035 --> 18:32.375
Curse my razor-sharp intuition...

275
18:32.705 --> 18:34.945
You're just completely tactless, you know that?

276
18:36.815 --> 18:41.415
Sae-chan, you have someone?

277
18:43.815 --> 18:45.185
You were here?

278
18:46.255 --> 18:48.125
Yeah, pretty much.

279
18:48.475 --> 18:49.825
Is that a problem?

280
18:50.355 --> 18:51.355
Huh?

281
18:51.625 --> 18:54.224
A huge problem!

282
18:54.225 --> 18:57.595
You're two years younger than me, and you already have a boyfriend?!

283
18:58.835 --> 18:59.835
I mean,

284
19:01.775 --> 19:03.504
in my entire life,

285
19:03.505 --> 19:06.805
I've never even had a boyfriend!

286
19:08.345 --> 19:09.714
What does that make me?!

287
19:09.715 --> 19:12.485
Wait, Yuria-san is older than me?

288
19:13.535 --> 19:15.815
Uh, don't look at me. How should I know...?

289
19:17.435 --> 19:18.435
Hey,

290
19:18.795 --> 19:20.855
thanks for helping me back there.

291
19:21.015 --> 19:22.424
For changing the subject, I mean.

292
19:22.425 --> 19:23.425
Hm?

293
19:24.155 --> 19:27.065
I really didn't want to talk about my relationship.

294
19:30.095 --> 19:31.335
Wait a second...

295
19:31.735 --> 19:33.735
Why are you suddenly using polite speech?

296
19:34.065 --> 19:35.075
Well,

297
19:35.335 --> 19:37.235
I didn't know you were older than me.

298
19:38.445 --> 19:39.645
Oh, come on!

299
19:39.905 --> 19:41.374
Don't worry about that!

300
19:41.375 --> 19:42.921
You're the senior worker here, Sae-chan!

301
19:42.945 --> 19:45.545
Aren't you speaking politely too, Yuria-san?

302
19:45.645 --> 19:47.815
Oh, I know!

303
19:48.215 --> 19:50.115
Let's both just talk casually!

304
19:50.215 --> 19:53.034
Uh, I'd rather not.

305
19:53.035 --> 19:54.035
Come on!

306
19:54.085 --> 19:56.425
You're supposed to listen to your elders!

307
19:56.855 --> 19:59.695
Pulling the age card now of all times?

308
20:02.795 --> 20:04.534
You're hilarious, Sae-chan!

309
20:04.535 --> 20:06.665
You're the funny one here.

310
20:23.761 --> 20:25.867
(Miwa: What about tomorrow?)

311
20:33.405 --> 20:40.205
(Saeko: Worked six days straight and I'm exhausted. I'm staying home to rest tomorrow.)

312
20:51.215 --> 20:53.615
Put it next to the griddle. Right here. Over here.

313
20:53.635 --> 20:55.155
Here, Tsuruta, take this.

314
20:55.215 --> 20:56.215
Huh?

315
20:56.555 --> 20:57.914
Not this one.

316
20:57.915 --> 21:00.085
- Huh? - Not that.

317
21:00.335 --> 21:02.924
- But you said the green one! - No, take this back to the club room.

318
21:02.925 --> 21:04.625
Oh, man, seriously?

319
21:04.755 --> 21:05.755
Saeko?

320
21:07.061 --> 21:07.463
Yeah?

321
21:07.487 --> 21:09.418
Can you help me carry this box back to the club room?

322
21:09.835 --> 21:12.935
Whoa, that looks crazy heavy.

323
21:13.305 --> 21:15.175
Please! I'm dying here.

324
21:16.735 --> 21:18.694
- I've hit my limit... Can't take it. - Hey, Lucha.

325
21:18.695 --> 21:20.245
Give it a rest.

326
21:20.675 --> 21:22.814
- Ah, so heavy! - Do it yourself, Lucha.

327
21:22.815 --> 21:24.344
I've been busting my butt here too, you know!

328
21:24.345 --> 21:26.285
Saeko, want some help?

329
21:29.335 --> 21:30.335
Oh.

330
21:30.355 --> 21:32.485
Really? You're a lifesaver.

331
21:36.325 --> 21:39.695
Feels like it's been ages since we were alone together.

332
21:40.595 --> 21:41.595
Has it?

333
21:42.795 --> 21:44.035
It has.

334
21:44.195 --> 21:46.435
You've been working shifts non-stop.

335
21:48.235 --> 21:50.775
A new hire started recently,

336
21:50.805 --> 21:53.775
so I ended up having to train her.

337
21:54.475 --> 21:55.715
I see.

338
21:58.185 --> 21:59.185
Here, let me carry that.

339
21:59.445 --> 22:01.234
Oh, it's fine. I've got it.

340
22:01.235 --> 22:02.555
No, really.

341
22:15.035 --> 22:16.235
Let's head back.

342
22:18.205 --> 22:19.405
Saeko...

343
22:19.805 --> 22:23.674
Saeko... have you been avoiding me lately?

344
22:23.675 --> 22:24.535
What?

345
22:24.575 --> 22:25.905
You're overthinking things.

346
22:26.075 --> 22:28.215
I am not.

347
22:29.935 --> 22:30.935
Even if I were...

348
22:31.115 --> 22:33.044
isn't everything fine the way it is?

349
22:33.045 --> 22:34.361
We're getting along totally normally, aren't we?

350
22:34.385 --> 22:36.214
It's not fine at all.

351
22:36.215 --> 22:37.814
If something's wrong, just talk to me.

352
22:37.815 --> 22:39.685
I told you, nothing is wrong!

353
22:41.525 --> 22:42.525
Don't be like this.

354
22:42.526 --> 22:44.395
There's clearly something going on.

355
22:45.195 --> 22:46.195
Please.

356
22:46.196 --> 22:47.665
Can't we just talk?

357
22:50.395 --> 22:52.535
I already told you, I'm fine.

358
22:54.935 --> 22:57.535
You always brush me off like this.

359
22:58.105 --> 23:00.345
Tell me what you really think so we can talk it through.

360
23:00.375 --> 23:01.715
Aren't we in a relationship?

361
23:03.215 --> 23:04.215
What?

362
23:04.345 --> 23:05.445
What I really think?

363
23:07.385 --> 23:08.815
Whose real thoughts?

364
23:08.855 --> 23:10.155
Mine?

365
23:11.855 --> 23:14.055
Quit playing the innocent victim!

366
23:14.855 --> 23:17.455
You're the one whose feelings wandered first!

367
23:17.655 --> 23:19.965
Did you really think I wouldn't notice?

368
23:24.365 --> 23:28.405
Did you honestly think you could just play me for a fool?!

369
23:43.685 --> 23:44.965
(Next Episode Preview) We were...

370
23:45.155 --> 23:47.114
always getting along so well, weren't we?

371
23:47.115 --> 23:49.225
Let's lay it all out in the open.

372
23:49.255 --> 23:51.174
Are you doing all right over there?

373
23:51.175 --> 23:52.375
In this whole world,

374
23:52.595 --> 23:56.065
it feels like I'm the only one who isn't loved by anyone.

375
23:56.095 --> 23:57.595
Damn it.
